  "statement": "A courier starts at depot city 0, must visit every one of the other cities exactly once, and must come back to city 0. Going directly from city i to city j costs d[i][j]; the costs are not necessarily symmetric (d[i][j] may differ from d[j][i]). Print the minimum total cost of such a round trip.\n\nInput: the first line holds n, the number of cities (numbered 0..n-1). Each of the next n lines holds n integers: line i gives d[i][0] .. d[i][n-1]. d[i][i] is always 0.\nOutput: one integer, the minimum cost. With n = 1 the courier never moves and the answer is 0.\n\nConstraints: 1 <= n <= 18, 0 <= d[i][j] <= 1000000. Trying every order of the cities is far too slow for n = 18.\n\nExample:\nInput:\n4\n0 10 15 20\n5 0 9 10\n6 13 0 12\n8 8 9 0\nOutput:\n35\nOne best route is 0 -> 1 -> 3 -> 2 -> 0, costing 10 + 10 + 9 + 6 = 35.",
  "starter_code": "import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(in.readLine().trim());\n        int[][] d = new int[n][n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) d[i][j] = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        }\n        // Print the cheapest round trip from city 0\n    }\n}\n",
